  "notes": "The only half-time-first model in this batch — `halfTime` true, clap on 3, 118–126 — and the lazy feel is authored rather than described: `quantizeStrength` 0.72 with 8–11 ms of jitter on the snare and clap plus `offGridMs` 9, which is the largest deliberate lateness here. The Chattanooga half of the sensibility lands on the harmony: real motion (i–iv–VII–III and the Imaj7–vi7 soul cycle) with seventh 0.5 and ninth 0.22, against a lane whose median is a two-chord vamp. Two more parameters are his and nobody else’s in this batch: `bass808.melodicallyIndependent` with `bassline.rhythm` independent_riff at `followRootsProb` 0.55, because the research says the bass doubles the sample’s root motion rather than the kick; and `sectionRules.outro.decay` false, because the research says tracks end on a loop rather than a resolve. The vinyl-noise and tape-hiss bed is the `percs` lane list, and it is the reason `percs.densityPerBar` stays [1,3] under a sparse kit. ⚠ `medium`: the research rates tempo/key medium-high and drum detail medium. The inferred parameter is the hat programming — “lose 16ths with triplet fills” is a description, and the specific `fillDensity` 0.38 and the 16th base are the reading of it. ⚠ **`lockTo808` raised from 0.4 to 0.61.** The 808 takes each kick with this probability, and at 0.4 over this model's 8-kick floor a seed could produce no 808 at all — which `bass808.rs` refuses, because a declared 808 that sometimes vanishes is a part a producer cannot rely on. It is still well under a lock: a good share of kicks carry no sub. ⚠ The bass ceiling came down from 47 to 43 so it stays under a chord part that starts at 44 — `coherence.rs` requires the highest bass note to sit at or below the lowest chord note, and this model overlapped by 4.",
